\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Identification ranges in the retained sixteen-city, ten-indicator matrix. Eight of the eleven fully unknown entries concern upper-secondary pupil--teacher ratios. Shading shows utility upper minus lower bounds; dots mark retained point assumptions and question marks identify $[0,1]$ entries. Point assumptions include submitted values and do not certify independent validation or zero measurement error. These are identification bounds under the retained source rules, not confidence intervals. Travel entries retain school-travel and general-commute proxy scopes. Cities follow the input order. Source: V205 utility bounds.}}{9}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
