\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces Modelled walking time to 20 generic Learning POIs in retained resident cells. Colours and heights use a common 0--150 minute scale; height is not terrain. Percentages weight cells with mean time at most 30 minutes by retained residents. Grids were captured on 10 November (Oslo) and 7 November 2026 (Zurich); input years are unstated and boundaries differ \cite  {brunogrids}. Oslo's retained 686,862 residents differ from the primary population of 727,797. Three Oslo NASA HLS requests were transparent, so its backdrop is geometry only. Zurich's requested 27 June 2024 background is cloudy; the granule date is unverified \cite  {nasagibs}. Neither panel measures student, high-school or pool access.}}{16}{figure.3}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:walktime-context}{{3}{16}{Modelled walking time to 20 generic Learning POIs in retained resident cells. Colours and heights use a common 0--150 minute scale; height is not terrain. Percentages weight cells with mean time at most 30 minutes by retained residents. Grids were captured on 10 November (Oslo) and 7 November 2026 (Zurich); input years are unstated and boundaries differ \cite {brunogrids}. Oslo's retained 686,862 residents differ from the primary population of 727,797. Three Oslo NASA HLS requests were transparent, so its backdrop is geometry only. Zurich's requested 27 June 2024 background is cloudy; the granule date is unverified \cite {nasagibs}. Neither panel measures student, high-school or pool access}{figure.3}{}}
